      "subject": "Add Redis rate limiting and order.created events",
      "body": ""
    }
  ],
  "description": {
    "file": "description.md",
    "text": "Rate limiting for the Orders API\n\nSomeone hammering POST /orders can take the API down. This limits each visitor to 20 orders a minute, counted in Redis so every server shares the count, and answers the 21st with a 429 and a Retry-After header.\n\nAlso: orders are priced from the pricing module instead of a flat 10 per item, an empty order is refused, and a new order publishes order.created to the queue. The old in-memory throttle is deleted, since nothing used it."
  },
